":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer reaches the central conclusion: appointing a principal underwriter is a legal and operational distribution role and does not assure a sales force or asset gathering. It covers both required distinctions. Salespeople, wholesaling and marketing are described as separately contracted. Intermediary access (wirehouse, RIA and model-provider approvals) is described as separate relationship work. It also says platform packages differ and should not be assumed identical. It does not wrongly claim that every sponsor must employ its own sales team. It omits the Simplify/Foreside example and the detail that the distributor's fee is paid from the adviser's resources, but these are incidental. Attributing creation/redemption processing and AP coordination to the underwriter is a reasonable generalization of ETF distributor functions, not a material error.\"}","ttft_ms":2248,"type":"result","duration_ms":4482,"uuid":"61c4baf3-cbc7-4d91-832d-6198e0bf23c5","ttft_stream_ms":578,"time_to_request_ms":55,"first_content_frame_ms":578,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
